You feel spoiled.

	It depends on which version of the game you're playing.  If you're
playing version 3.1.x (the latest version), your carrying ability depends on
the average of your STR and your CON.  The equation looks like this;

	Capacity=20 units*[(STR +CON)/2 +1].

For the purpose of this equation, 18/** STR is equivalent to 21 STR.  In
addition, there is a hard maximum of 1000 units, so if your Constitution is 17
or greater, it doesn't matter.

	In version 3.0j, it depends entirely on whether your game has the HARD
option compiled into it.

>Is a wand of speed monster useful on the pet ?

	Yes, if you like having a speedy pet.  Try zapping it on yourself.
It's much more useful that way.

>What are the best monsters to polymorph into ?

	That's mostly a matter of personal preference.  My favorites are the
Vampire Lord and the Master Lich, since they are tough customers and can wear
body armor.  If you're not concerned about armor, try a Balrog or an Archon.

>When polymorphed into a monster which can lay an egg, will be the egg become
>another monster pet after time ?

	No, unless you had polymorphed into a chameleon.

